{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Ratchet `Any` and loose typing repo-wide (re-scoped against current main)\n\n## Premise re-validated on main @ ea6ee67e6a (measured, not assumed)\n\nThe original description's baseline is stale. Re-measured today with\n`mypy src/rebar/<pkg> --disallow-untyped-defs` (repo settings) and\n`--disallow-any-explicit`:\n\n| package | untyped-def errors | +explicit-Any errors |\n|---|---|---|\n| attest, graph, grounding, metrics | 0 | 2 / 15 / 116 / 76 |\n| _snapshot, _store, reducer | 1 | 0 / 17 / 5 |\n| schemas | 2 | 5 |\n| opcert_service, review_bot | 3 | 1 / 42 |\n| _io, _engine_support | 4 | 8 / 7 |\n| audit | 7 | 15 |\n| _cli | 11 | 0 |\n| _engine | 134 | large |\n| _commands | 146 | large |\n| llm | 293 | large |\n\nTwo facts change the scope:\n\n1. Sibling `abasic-doddering-harrier` (9efe) annotated `attest` and **explicitly deferred\n   the one-line ratchet promotion to this ticket**; `metrics` is *also* already clean and\n   was never promoted. Both flips are free today.\n2. The gap between \"already in the ratchet\" (`rebar.graph.*`, `rebar.grounding.*` in\n   `pyproject.toml`) and \"already clean\" is **12 packages**, and 10 of those are within\n   **37 trivial annotations** total. The genuinely hard residue is only\n   `llm` / `_commands` / `_engine` (573 untyped defs, ~389 explicit `Any`).\n\nSo the ticket's own AC #2 (\"extend the ratchet to constrain `Any`\") is achievable **with\nmypy's own `disallow_any_explicit`** rather than a bespoke counter: `_cli` and `_snapshot`\nmeasure at **zero** explicit-`Any` errors, so they can carry both flags as the worked\nexample. Reducing `Any` in `llm`/`_engine` and converting the reconciler transport port\nend-to-end are NOT trivially small and are split out (below), not attempted here.\n\n## Plan\n\n**A. Annotate the 37 remaining untyped defs (annotations only, no behaviour change, no new `Any`).**\nEvery one is a missing return type or an un-annotated `repo_root=None` / `args` / callback\nparameter:\n- `rebar._snapshot.cache.open_in_snapshot`, `rebar._store.hlc._hlc_lock`,\n  `rebar.reducer._filters.match_predicate` (the `value` param).\n- `rebar.schemas.registry`, `rebar.schemas.validator`.\n- `rebar.opcert_service.jobs.run_job` / `_dispatch_completion` / `_dispatch_plan_review`\n  (the `fn` callbacks -> `Callable[...]`).\n- `rebar.review_bot.adapter._resolve_reviewed_head` / `_assert_reviewed_tree` /\n  `code_review_decision` (`repo_root`).\n- `rebar._io.import_ndjson.import_tickets`, `rebar._io.export_ndjson.export_tickets`,\n  `rebar._io._cli.export_cli` / `import_cli` (`repo_root`).\n- `rebar._engine_support.output._resolve_profile` / `error_envelope`,\n  `rebar._engine_support.bridge_fsck._load_classify` (-> `ModuleType`).\n- `rebar.audit.read.plan_review_health` / `_completion_attestation` /\n  `_completion_sidecar_record` / `_related_code_reviews` / `audit_trail` / `rebar_show`,\n  `rebar.audit.server._render_ticket` (all `repo_root`).\n- `rebar._cli._llm_eval_commands._prompt_eval` / `_criteria_eval` / `_pct` / `_llm_setup`,\n  `rebar._cli._workflow_commands._workflow_{edit,show,run,read,new,validate}`,\n  `rebar._cli._bridge_commands._ref_lock_module` (`args` -> `argparse.Namespace`).\n\nAll 14 touched files are 127-684 LOC; none is near the 800 cap, and no file gains more\nthan ~11 lines. `llm/pass1.py` and `_lib_writes.py` are NOT touched.\n\n**B. Promote every now-clean package in `pyproject.toml`** into the existing\n`[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` `disallow_untyped_defs` block: `rebar.attest.*`,\n`rebar.metrics.*`, `rebar._snapshot.*`, `rebar._store.*`, `rebar.reducer.*`,\n`rebar.schemas.*`, `rebar.opcert_service.*`, `rebar.review_bot.*`, `rebar._io.*`,\n`rebar._engine_support.*`, `rebar.audit.*`, `rebar._cli.*` (2 -> 14 packages).\n\n**C. Extend the ratchet to constrain `Any`** — a SECOND override block with\n`disallow_any_explicit = true` for the packages measured clean under it\n(`rebar._cli.*`, `rebar._snapshot.*`), re-verified after step A. This is the mechanism the\nticket asks for, built from existing machinery, not a parallel one.\n\n**D. Guard it, shrink-only, in `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py`.** Grow\n`_RATCHET_BASELINE` to the 14 promoted packages, and add `_ANY_RATCHET_BASELINE` plus a\n`test_any_ratchet_strict_set_only_grows` mirroring the existing subset assertion, so the\n`Any` tier can only ever grow. `disallow_any_explicit` is added to the existing\n`_DEFERRED_GLOBAL_FLAGS`-style check as an override-only flag (never a global key).\n\n**E. Record it in `docs/architecture.md`** (\"mypy strictness ratchet\" section): that\n`disallow_untyped_defs` is satisfied by `: Any` and therefore delivers neither driver, the\ntwo-tier ratchet (untyped-def tier + explicit-`Any` tier), and the measured\nbefore/after table above as the baseline the tiers shrink from.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope -> `discovered_from` follow-ups filed before close\n\n- `llm` / `_commands` / `_engine` annotation + `Any` reduction (573 untyped defs, ~389\n  explicit `Any`) — epic-sized, and `llm/pass1.py` is at the module-size cap.\n- The reconciler transport port converted end-to-end with a Serena reference-finding\n  measurement (already scoped by `cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8`; blocked on the same near-cap\n  files).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (refined; supersedes the provisional list)\n\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/<pkg> --disallow-untyped-defs` is clean for all 14 packages named in\n      step B, and `pyproject.toml` lists exactly those 14 in the `disallow_untyped_defs`\n      override (2 before, 14 after).\n- [ ] A second `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` block sets `disallow_any_explicit = true` for\n      `rebar._cli.*` and `rebar._snapshot.*`, and\n      `mypy src/rebar/_cli src/rebar/_snapshot --disallow-untyped-defs --disallow-any-explicit`\n      is clean — i.e. the ratchet now constrains `Any`, not only unannotated defs.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py` pins BOTH tiers as shrink-only (removing any\n      package from either list turns the build red), verified by running the test.\n- [ ] The annotation work adds **no new `: Any` / `-> Any`**: repo-wide count of\n      `grep -rnE ':\\s*Any\\b|->\\s*Any\\b' src/rebar` is unchanged from the pre-change value\n      (machine-checked, same oracle sibling 9efe used).\n- [ ] `docs/architecture.md` records the `Any`-blindness of `disallow_untyped_defs`, the\n      two-tier ratchet, and the measured per-package baseline table.\n- [ ] Full local gate set green (ten `check_*` gates, generators no-diff, `make lint`,\n      `make typecheck`, CI pytest selection, `tests/integration`), and the change lands\n      `Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1`.\n- [ ] Follow-up tickets filed and linked `discovered_from` for the two out-of-scope items."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786647910424013001,"uuid":"80b9dc6e-bc5f-4889-9fac-3b755579d5d0"}